From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:49:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] A shaft of light is a light

Patch 0029 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

This game draws every beam of light the same way: a see-through shape with a soft fading
texture, long against its width and round across it, standing up or leaning in from above. The
pedestal beam in the Temple of Time, the shaft in every grotto and grave, the sprout's shaft in
the Deku Tree's meadow, the Forest and Spirit Temples' slanted beams, a warp's column. The
console lit nothing with them; the shaft only glowed, and in the Temple of Time a zone on the
floor switched the whole scene brighter, so a figure half inside the beam lit up whole (the
user, 2026-10-08: "he's partially inside of it, but his whole body is lit up, even the parts
that are outside of it").

Each traced scene's see-through draws are now measured as they are classified. A draw that
tests depth, samples a fading texture and has the shape of a shaft becomes a light: a cylinder
of light falling down its own axis, from the top of the shaft, as wide as the shaft is drawn at
each end, in the color the draw's own combiner gives it at its brightest. The local lights pass
lights only what stands inside the cylinder, from the direction it falls, with shadow rays back
up the shaft, and the edge of the shaft fades over its outer third. The air's glow leaves beams
out, because the shaft the game draws is the glow. Beams follow the game's lights in the list,
up to eight per scene, and a shaft drawn in layers is one beam.

The shape test comes from an inventory of every room in the game: long against its width (the
variance along the main axis at least four times what is left across it), round across it (the
smaller cross variance at least a quarter of the larger; the Temple of Time's is a third, the
grottos' whole, and every flat strip in the game, a waterfall, a band of light on a wall, under
a fifth), at least 150 units long, and upright or leaning from above. Shape rather than a list
of places, so an actor's beam is found the same way at any scale.

Rung 37 leaves every shaft as the game drew it, and takes the cut-out quads of patch 0027 like
the default, so it differs from Off only in this. The program reads the same rung to put back
the Temple of Time's floor switch.

